  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "iQKpYC55bWld7w8aXCz4u1Etn3A=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-30T18:30:20.694Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The **agentic economy** describes a financial system where AI agents autonomously hold balances, sign transactions, negotiate terms, and authorize payments with minimal human intervention. Microsoft researchers (Rothschild, Mobius, Hofman) formalized the concept in May 2025.\n\n**Key reframing:** when billions of agents represent consumers to businesses, *\"trust, and not attention, is now the scarce resource\"* \u2014 the attention economy's advertising logic doesn't work on software that can't be persuaded, only verified.\n\n**Why it matters:** it defines a new market structure where the customers, workers, and merchants can all be software.\n\nSource: LI.FI, \"The Agentic Economy \u2014 A Deep Dive\" (https://li.fi/knowledge-hub/the-agentic-economy-%E2%80%94-a-deep-dive).",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-30T12:10:00.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-30T18:30:20.694Z"
    }
  },
